# Getting started

This site is ready for documentation written in `.svx` files. Replace this page with your framework's introduction, installation instructions, and first example.

## Write documentation

Add `.svx` files under `src/content/docs`. Their paths become documentation URLs, and frontmatter controls the title, description, section, and order.

```text
---
title: Your first guide
description: Explain the first thing users should build.
section: Guides
order: 20
---

# Your first guide

Write ordinary Markdown and Svelte components here.
```

## Optional Rust API insights

The site works without Rustdoc data: fenced code blocks receive syntax highlighting. To add hover cards, source links, signatures, and searchable framework symbols, configure `src/lib/docs/config.ts` and prepare an artifact from your framework checkout:

```sh
bun run docs:prepare --local ../framework
```

Once prepared, framework identifiers in Rust code blocks are enriched automatically. You can also add focused handwritten API pages under `src/content/symbols` when a symbol needs deeper explanation.
